Cactus Code Thorn CapyrX_TestOuterBC
Author(s)    : Lucas Timotheo Sanches <lsanches@lsu.edu>
               Erik Schnetter <schnetter@gmail.com>

Maintainer(s): Lucas Timotheo Sanches <lsanches@lsu.edu>

Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

The two physical-outer-boundary diagnostics of the CapyrX multipatch test
suite:

  * the NaN-injection test, which injects NaN at (or just inside) the genuine
    physical outer boundary and asks whether it leaks across an interpatch
    interface; and

  * the smooth-field "Channel 1" A/B test, which fills a smooth analytic field
    everywhere -- outer-BC ghosts included -- and compares what an interpatch
    receiver reads under different CarpetX::boundary_* kinds.

Both used to live in CapyrX_TestMultiPatch behind its `run_outer_bc_tests`
parameter.  They were moved out because CarpetX allocates a MultiFab for every
DECLARED grid function whether or not any thorn asks for storage
(CarpetX/src/driver.cxx loops over CCTK_NumGroups() unconditionally, and
CarpetX's GroupStorageIncrease/Decrease in src/schedule.cxx are no-ops), and
it requires every such group to be VALID before it creates a refined level.
A group that is declared but written only by a switched-off diagnostic
therefore aborted the run at "MakeNewLevelFromCoarse before prolongation" the
moment CarpetX::max_num_levels > 1 -- which made every CapyrX_TestMultiPatch
par file, the coloring test included, unusable with mesh refinement.

Activating this thorn is now the switch.  When it is not in ActiveThorns the
four fields do not exist; when it is, its two routines write all four
unconditionally.  CapyrX_TestMultiPatch keeps `run_outer_bc_tests` and refuses
at PARAMCHECK if it is set while this thorn is inactive, so an old par file
fails by name with the line to add rather than silently producing nothing.

2. Parameters

  nan_injection_mode   where to inject NaN relative to the physical outer
                       boundary; moved here unchanged
  smooth_field         which analytic field the A/B test uses; moved here
                       unchanged
  smooth_sentinel      outer-BC ghost sentinel for the slaved-fill weight
                       measurement, 0 = off; moved here unchanged

3. Checkers

  scripts/check_nan_test.py and scripts/check_smooth_test.py, in
  CapyrX_TestMultiPatch, read this thorn's TSV output.  The output file names
  carry the thorn name, so they now begin `capyrx_testouterbc-`.
